1
00:02:15,406 --> 00:02:16,490
Anything?

2
00:02:16,574 --> 00:02:17,992
No one goes in or out.

3
00:02:18,075 --> 00:02:19,326
Figures.

4
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:22,371
Faraday was right. He changed sites.

5
00:02:22,454 --> 00:02:26,000
It was a lost cause.
Dropped the ball on this one.

6
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:29,503
Must be big if Arasaka's willing to
clean house over a stolen car.

7
00:02:29,587 --> 00:02:33,090
If only that Faraday'd tell us
what the fuck we after.

8
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:35,759
This stinks of high-risk shit.

9
00:02:35,843 --> 00:02:38,554
"The biggest fish is always
the one that got away"?

10
00:02:38,637 --> 00:02:41,015
Want me to dig deeper into Tanaka?

11
00:02:41,599 --> 00:02:47,646
Nah, sniffing around
‘Saka business is a fixer's job.

12
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:51,775
"You are being paid to check off
the boxes on my checklist."

13
00:02:51,859 --> 00:02:55,905
Yeah, yeah.
I went ahead and sicced Kiwi on him.

14
00:02:55,988 --> 00:02:58,741
I guess we'll see what we find.

15
00:02:58,824 --> 00:03:01,035
So we're on hold for now?

16
00:03:01,118 --> 00:03:05,539
We'll need to find a way to kill time…

17
00:03:43,118 --> 00:03:44,662
Said yourself, right?

18
00:03:45,579 --> 00:03:47,206
Alright, fine.

19
00:03:48,374 --> 00:03:50,042
I'm here for Aldo.

20
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:52,670
Yeah? Who's asking?

21
00:03:52,753 --> 00:03:54,463
Maine sent me.

22
00:03:54,546 --> 00:03:57,299
Hah? You Davis?

23
00:03:57,383 --> 00:03:58,842
Uh…

24
00:03:58,926 --> 00:03:59,802
Huh?

25
00:03:59,885 --> 00:04:01,178
I'm David.

26
00:04:01,262 --> 00:04:02,096
Davis?

27
00:04:02,179 --> 00:04:05,307
David! Not Davis! David!

28
00:04:05,391 --> 00:04:08,352
The fuck you screaming for?!
I can hear you.

29
00:04:08,435 --> 00:04:13,565
David? You're Pilar's carrier pigeon.

30
00:04:13,649 --> 00:04:14,692
Pilar's?

31
00:04:15,526 --> 00:04:21,448
Was you, wasn't it? The punk kid
who klepped and junked the ‘Saka limo?

32
00:04:21,532 --> 00:04:24,243
Yeah… First time on the job.

33
00:04:24,326 --> 00:04:30,708
Could've collected 5K for it at least
if you hadn't gone and trashed it to hell.

34
00:04:30,791 --> 00:04:32,626
-I'll remember that next time.
-Huh?

35
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:34,128
I'll do better next time!

36
00:04:35,754 --> 00:04:37,715
Next time, eh?

37
00:04:37,798 --> 00:04:41,760
Guess we'll see if last time wasn't
a stroke of beginner's luck.

38
00:04:41,844 --> 00:04:43,220
What do you mean?

39
00:04:43,304 --> 00:04:45,014
Nothing personal.

40
00:04:45,097 --> 00:04:49,351
Won't take long to see if
you're the shit or just a lil' shit stain.

41
00:04:50,311 --> 00:04:52,563
Hear about that cyberpsycho up in Watson?

42
00:04:52,646 --> 00:04:54,315
They just keep popping up.

43
00:04:54,398 --> 00:04:59,862
Yeah, took out two NCPD on patrol.
Saw the scroll. It was damn bloody.

44
00:04:59,945 --> 00:05:04,074
A single launcher hit
turned him into so much canned paste…

45
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:14,293
Hey David! How've you been?

46
00:05:14,376 --> 00:05:15,461
Uh…

47
00:05:15,544 --> 00:05:17,713
What's up? You need something?

48
00:05:17,796 --> 00:05:21,967
Uh. Got this package here
from Maine for Pilar.

49
00:05:22,051 --> 00:05:22,926
Oh…

50
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:24,345
Bro!

51
00:05:24,428 --> 00:05:25,888
Bro?

52
00:05:25,971 --> 00:05:28,057
Delivery from Maine!

53
00:05:29,183 --> 00:05:30,309
Fucking finally!

54
00:05:30,809 --> 00:05:35,439
You know how many of
the boys'd kill to get these cyberhands?

55
00:05:35,522 --> 00:05:37,608
Preeem!

56
00:05:39,735 --> 00:05:41,445
Need me to excuse you now, or…?

57
00:05:41,528 --> 00:05:43,864
He have anything else for me to do?

58
00:05:43,947 --> 00:05:45,657
Bro?

59
00:05:45,741 --> 00:05:50,788
Yeah, fuck off. Tip him on his way out.

60
00:05:50,871 --> 00:05:54,041
He's your errand boy!
Fork it over yourself, cheap-ass!

61
00:05:54,124 --> 00:05:55,000
It's bulletproof!

62
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:57,711
So do I clock out now?

63
00:05:57,795 --> 00:05:59,963
Uh… Looks that way.

64
00:06:00,047 --> 00:06:01,507
Oh. Cool…

65
00:06:02,883 --> 00:06:05,219
Whoa?! All this for a tip?!

66
00:06:05,803 --> 00:06:07,721
You're adorable.

67
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:10,432
See you later, David.

68
00:06:24,196 --> 00:06:25,823
You came?

69
00:06:25,906 --> 00:06:28,492
You told me to come.

70
00:06:28,575 --> 00:06:30,494
Maine bullied me into it.

71
00:06:30,577 --> 00:06:32,496
Wha… Maine?

72
00:06:50,305 --> 00:06:51,390
Asshole.

73
00:06:52,182 --> 00:06:53,183
You're kidding.

74
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:55,686
You're telling me. It's my day off.

75
00:06:55,769 --> 00:06:57,938
Sorry to hear it.

76
00:06:58,564 --> 00:07:02,359
No offense, but you're not
exactly built like a punk.

77
00:07:02,442 --> 00:07:07,322
You look like you'd tweak out
after one or two more implants.

78
00:07:07,406 --> 00:07:09,825
I'm not that weak!

79
00:07:09,908 --> 00:07:11,410
Keep up, then.

80
00:07:16,165 --> 00:07:17,958
Ever use one?

81
00:07:18,041 --> 00:07:19,251
No.

82
00:07:19,334 --> 00:07:23,464
Gloria never let you carry?
Well, better start now than never.

83
00:07:23,547 --> 00:07:26,091
Could teach ya if ya want.

84
00:07:26,675 --> 00:07:30,262
Think I'll stick with the Sandevistan.

85
00:07:52,993 --> 00:07:54,036
Hey.

86
00:07:54,119 --> 00:07:54,953
Yes?

87
00:07:55,537 --> 00:07:58,165
So, you're a netrunner?

88
00:07:58,248 --> 00:07:59,500
Yeah. And?

89
00:07:59,583 --> 00:08:02,836
Nothing. Just… do netrunners need to run?

90
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:07,382
Netrunner, edgerunner. No difference.
Stamina is everything.

91
00:08:36,495 --> 00:08:40,123
Don't leave the house empty-handed
from now on, you hear me?

92
00:08:40,999 --> 00:08:44,920
Every day. You check for your wallet,
your condom, and your gun.

93
00:08:45,504 --> 00:08:49,216
Sure, some punks go straight chrome.

94
00:08:49,299 --> 00:08:54,429
But it's gonna be a while before you can
stay alive with just your cyberware.

95
00:08:55,013 --> 00:08:58,934
Until then, that gun's gonna be
your backup plan.

96
00:09:05,691 --> 00:09:06,775
Hey.

97
00:09:06,858 --> 00:09:07,818
Yes?

98
00:09:07,901 --> 00:09:09,528
How old are you anyway?

99
00:09:35,512 --> 00:09:37,014
How're things with Lucy?

100
00:09:37,097 --> 00:09:38,056
Huh?

101
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,433
You treating her right?

102
00:09:40,309 --> 00:09:46,023
No, I didn't mean… Well, your age
and skills don't really add up.

103
00:09:46,106 --> 00:09:48,358
Skill has nothing to do with age.

104
00:09:48,442 --> 00:09:50,319
It's all about hard work.

105
00:09:50,402 --> 00:09:54,197
Besides, only idiots talk down to
people younger than them.

106
00:09:54,281 --> 00:09:55,657
Like who?

107
00:09:55,741 --> 00:09:57,451
Like long-armed techies.

108
00:10:21,767 --> 00:10:23,852
What do you mean "treating her right"?

109
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:26,605
Wait… You still haven't done it?

110
00:10:26,688 --> 00:10:28,982
What are we talking about exactly?

111
00:10:29,066 --> 00:10:32,944
David, you're gonna need to
grow a pair of cajones

112
00:10:33,028 --> 00:10:36,448
and I ain't just talking
in a cyberpunk sense.

113
00:10:39,534 --> 00:10:42,245
Thought I saw you two
talking the other day.

114
00:10:43,372 --> 00:10:46,333
At the party after the limo heist.

115
00:10:46,416 --> 00:10:49,836
He likes to act like
my mentor or something.

116
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:53,840
He got grabby, so I fried him a bit
and told him to scram.

117
00:10:53,924 --> 00:10:55,092
Huh.

118
00:10:56,385 --> 00:10:57,844
How about you?

119
00:10:58,428 --> 00:11:00,681
You serious about edgerunning?

120
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,607
I'm not into her like that.

121
00:11:11,191 --> 00:11:13,360
C'mon kid, we've all got eyes.

122
00:11:14,403 --> 00:11:17,823
She's not into me like that.

123
00:11:17,906 --> 00:11:19,199
Yeah, probably.

124
00:11:29,501 --> 00:11:30,502
Why are you asking?

125
00:11:30,585 --> 00:11:33,422
You just don't seem the type.

126
00:11:34,005 --> 00:11:35,006
Why?!

127
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:36,425
Tell me!

128
00:11:47,602 --> 00:11:51,273
I just don't know how much of it was real.

129
00:11:52,149 --> 00:11:53,024
What you mean?

130
00:11:53,608 --> 00:11:55,610
Said she wants to go to the moon.

131
00:11:55,694 --> 00:11:56,987
The moon?

132
00:11:57,070 --> 00:11:59,197
Yeah, it's her dream or whatever.

133
00:12:27,058 --> 00:12:28,727
You're faster than you look.

134
00:12:28,810 --> 00:12:30,604
Yeah, yeah.

135
00:12:30,687 --> 00:12:33,732
Really. Doubted you could keep up.

136
00:12:33,815 --> 00:12:37,486
Sarcasm? I'm not that easy to get rid of.

137
00:13:15,899 --> 00:13:18,485
Never said nothing about that to me.

138
00:13:19,194 --> 00:13:20,570
So she lied?

139
00:13:20,654 --> 00:13:22,989
Who knows? Just ask her.

140
00:13:23,073 --> 00:13:27,410
She was probably just stalling me, but…

141
00:13:27,494 --> 00:13:32,207
But we went to the moon together.
With her special BD.

142
00:13:32,290 --> 00:13:34,125
You had a date on the moon?

143
00:13:34,209 --> 00:13:38,380
Shit, you don't get much more
romantic than that in Night City.

144
00:13:47,597 --> 00:13:49,266
Here, a training regimen.

145
00:13:50,267 --> 00:13:54,354
This is just the bare minimum.
You're on your own after today.

146
00:13:55,188 --> 00:13:58,858
If you're serious about this,
you'll need to keep up. And then…

147
00:13:59,693 --> 00:14:00,735
And then?

148
00:14:22,048 --> 00:14:24,175
How long has she been with you guys?

149
00:14:25,051 --> 00:14:28,972
Been about a year? Kiwi brought her in.

150
00:14:29,055 --> 00:14:31,850
Said she found a natural.

151
00:14:31,933 --> 00:14:33,101
What about before that?

152
00:14:33,184 --> 00:14:36,563
I don't know.
Like I said, ask her yourself.

153
00:14:37,147 --> 00:14:39,399
I don't give two shits
about people's pasts

154
00:14:39,482 --> 00:14:42,527
so long as they can pull their weight.

155
00:14:42,611 --> 00:14:44,529
Thought you'd say that.

156
00:15:07,969 --> 00:15:09,471
'Ey, keep it down!

157
00:15:11,056 --> 00:15:12,265
Damn!

158
00:15:15,101 --> 00:15:16,853
Jeez, that's loud.

159
00:15:16,937 --> 00:15:17,771
Gross.

160
00:15:17,854 --> 00:15:18,730
Seriously.

161
00:15:18,813 --> 00:15:21,274
What's your problem, eh?

162
00:15:21,358 --> 00:15:23,109
Why you pissing in the street?!

163
00:15:23,693 --> 00:15:25,862
'Ey, homie! You hear me?!

164
00:15:25,946 --> 00:15:27,238
Leave him alone.

165
00:15:27,322 --> 00:15:28,365
Bye bro.

166
00:15:29,157 --> 00:15:30,700
You aiming for hole-in-one?

167
00:15:31,451 --> 00:15:33,745
I'm talking to ya! Ya hear me?!

168
00:15:33,828 --> 00:15:39,751
Listen, we don't like
walking in piss, asshole.

169
00:15:39,834 --> 00:15:44,673
Alright? This sidewalk belongs to us…

170
00:15:44,756 --> 00:15:49,636
Oh, shit! That's one hell of an implant!

171
00:15:50,595 --> 00:15:53,098
Gives whole new meaning to
the phrase "hard as ir--"

172
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,368
Hey…

173
00:16:17,706 --> 00:16:19,874
Da…

174
00:16:19,958 --> 00:16:23,086
vid…

175
00:16:24,462 --> 00:16:26,256
move…

176
00:16:49,571 --> 00:16:51,406
Not the time to freeze, kid!

177
00:16:51,489 --> 00:16:52,532
Fucking capped him!

178
00:16:52,615 --> 00:16:54,367
-Got bits of Pilar on me…
-Gimme that!

179
00:16:54,451 --> 00:16:57,037
Fucker!

180
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,496
You had no fucking right!

181
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:01,750
Fucking psycho trash!

182
00:17:04,335 --> 00:17:07,255
Stupid, you'll flatline
faster than you can land a shot!

183
00:17:07,338 --> 00:17:08,757
Let me go!

184
00:17:11,134 --> 00:17:12,177
Die!

185
00:17:17,807 --> 00:17:19,434
Shit, of all times…

186
00:17:20,018 --> 00:17:22,020
Kiwi! Reset Becca's system!

187
00:17:22,103 --> 00:17:23,188
On it.

188
00:17:27,192 --> 00:17:28,234
Where's Lucy?!

189
00:17:39,662 --> 00:17:41,623
Hey, asshole!

190
00:17:43,583 --> 00:17:44,501
David!

191
00:18:01,601 --> 00:18:03,019
Lucy!

192
00:18:04,854 --> 00:18:05,939
I'm alright.

193
00:18:06,606 --> 00:18:08,024
Good.

194
00:18:10,193 --> 00:18:11,027
You're bleeding…

195
00:18:18,618 --> 00:18:23,414
I'm the only one
who was allowed to kill him…

196
00:18:27,544 --> 00:18:28,962
Don't touch me.

197
00:18:29,045 --> 00:18:30,922
Do you need medical?

198
00:18:31,005 --> 00:18:31,965
No.

199
00:18:32,048 --> 00:18:35,593
Dorio, take Lucy to see a ripperdoc.

200
00:18:36,219 --> 00:18:39,931
I'll stay with Kiwi until the pigs arrive.

201
00:18:40,014 --> 00:18:43,351
Someone's gotta explain this mess.

202
00:18:43,434 --> 00:18:44,936
You heard him.

203
00:18:46,437 --> 00:18:49,107
You go with 'em, kid.

204
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:50,066
Huh?

205
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:55,029
We'll tell 'em we took him
out after he zeroed Pilar.

206
00:18:55,113 --> 00:18:58,533
They'll file it as a cyberpsycho incident,
but it's better that you ain't here.

207
00:18:58,616 --> 00:18:59,450
But…

208
00:18:59,534 --> 00:19:01,369
I saw what you did.

209
00:19:01,452 --> 00:19:03,997
Time you stopped thinking like a rookie.

210
00:19:06,082 --> 00:19:10,336
You lot again? I'm not actually
a licensed physicist, you know.

211
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:13,464
I didn't volunteer to come either.

212
00:19:13,548 --> 00:19:15,175
Charming.

213
00:19:15,258 --> 00:19:16,509
I'll go alone.

214
00:19:17,385 --> 00:19:20,096
Clean her up and get her home.

215
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:23,224
-You're leaving?
-Maine said you could take his car.

216
00:19:30,899 --> 00:19:32,025
Lucy.

217
00:19:42,410 --> 00:19:44,245
-Here's fine.
-Sure.

218
00:19:44,329 --> 00:19:45,246
Good night.

219
00:19:45,872 --> 00:19:50,376
Um… Can we talk?

220
00:19:54,839 --> 00:19:56,049
This way.

221
00:20:00,345 --> 00:20:02,931
Aw. It's all cloudy.

222
00:20:03,014 --> 00:20:07,060
That moon BD you showed me
was pretty sweet.

223
00:20:12,690 --> 00:20:15,318
I had something
I wanted to talk about, too.

224
00:20:15,401 --> 00:20:16,277
Oh?

225
00:20:16,361 --> 00:20:21,449
I know how it must look but…
What I told you that day before?

226
00:20:21,532 --> 00:20:24,661
I wasn't lying.
It was the first time I told anyone.

227
00:20:24,744 --> 00:20:25,787
That's…

228
00:20:25,870 --> 00:20:29,791
That's good.
I didn't want to think you were lying.

229
00:20:30,416 --> 00:20:32,043
What if I'm lying now?

230
00:20:32,126 --> 00:20:34,295
-I don't think you are.
-Why not?

231
00:20:34,379 --> 00:20:37,048
-'Cause I don't like that.
-That's crazy.

232
00:20:37,131 --> 00:20:39,676
You should've said something earlier.

233
00:20:39,759 --> 00:20:41,427
I couldn't.

234
00:20:41,511 --> 00:20:42,428
Why not?

235
00:20:43,012 --> 00:20:44,681
You were so mad at me.

236
00:20:44,764 --> 00:20:46,057
I wasn't mad.

237
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:48,059
Was too.

238
00:20:48,142 --> 00:20:52,313
I wasn't mad, just…
Well, yeah. Guess I was.

239
00:20:52,397 --> 00:20:53,564
See?

240
00:20:53,648 --> 00:20:55,566
I was angry, but…

241
00:20:55,650 --> 00:20:57,568
I wasn't pissed at you.

242
00:20:59,654 --> 00:21:01,823
Wouldn't have saved you if I did.

243
00:21:01,906 --> 00:21:03,574
-Liar.
-I'm not.

244
00:21:03,658 --> 00:21:04,701
No, that's a lie.

245
00:21:04,784 --> 00:21:11,249
You're the kind of guy who'll jump in fire
to save someone, even if you get burned.

246
00:21:11,958 --> 00:21:13,543
You're that type.

247
00:21:14,544 --> 00:21:16,921
Is that why you think I won't make it?

248
00:21:17,505 --> 00:21:20,300
Maine thinks I will. Why can't…

249
00:21:20,383 --> 00:21:24,846
No, it's not that. You'd make
a good edgerunner, I think.

250
00:21:25,638 --> 00:21:27,598
I really do.

251
00:21:27,682 --> 00:21:29,017
So what's the problem?

252
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:32,979
You don't make a name
as a cyberpunk by how you live.

253
00:21:34,022 --> 00:21:35,648
You're remembered by how you die.

254
00:21:37,734 --> 00:21:40,069
It's not the life or the end you deserve.

255
00:21:40,153 --> 00:21:43,281
What makes me any different from you?

256
00:21:43,364 --> 00:21:46,034
I have nowhere else to go.

257
00:21:46,117 --> 00:21:47,410
I don't either.

258
00:21:47,493 --> 00:21:49,203
You and I are worlds apart.

259
00:21:49,287 --> 00:21:50,580
How?!

260
00:21:54,083 --> 00:21:56,252
I'll take you to the moon!

261
00:21:58,087 --> 00:21:59,714
I promise!

262
00:22:09,599 --> 00:22:11,517
I just don't want you to die.

263
00:22:29,827 --> 00:22:31,412
I won't.
